['Professional Development',['Transform your team’s outlook & expertise on integrating nature connection into curriculum','Begin to instill a personal connection with the natural world, which translates into wonder and curiosity, that is contagious with students','Learn about your school’s surrounding ecosystem','Discover how to bring the outdoors inside your classrooms','Build community and connection among your faculty']],
['School Day Specials',['Wayfinders will join your community during the school day on a monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, or annual basis to provide seasonal, nature connection & SEL programming','Programs run through the grades with age-based curriculum','Customization opportunities are available','Support staff must be present and engaged']],
['Extended Day',['Supplement and differentiate your program by offering Wayfinders nature connection as part of your “lunch bunch” or after school enrichment program throughout the school year','Support staff must be present and engaged']],
['Field Trips',['Customized experiences based on curricular interests focused on nature, SEL, and seasonally-based themes','Trips can be as close as in the woods outside of your school or at one of our many outdoor locations']],
['Family Circles',['Wayfinders builds community through facilitated programs for school families on a monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, or annual basis to provide seasonal, nature connection & SEL programming.','Option 1: Facilitated parent/caregiver groups happen in tandem with children’s programming so parents/caregivers can catch their breath while connecting more deeply with others in their new community, and exploring parent/caregiver & community issues. Children engage in a nature connection/SEL activity during parent/caregiver groups.','Option 2: Facilitated parent/caregiver groups offer the option for parents/caregivers to connect alongside their children in nature. These experiences will help create the foundation for a long term family connection in and with nature.']],
['Caregiver & Me',['Wayfinders supports building community for new parents through weekly facilitated meet-ups where new parents/guardians/caregivers bond while their babies (under 2 years old) experience sensory play in nature to build their relationship with nature.']],
];
const approaches=[['One-on-one activities like pair shares','This game of “Shapeshifter” got teachers and administrators to hone their observation schools in preparation for supporting advisees through the Advisory Program.'],['Contemplative activities like "sit spot" and journaling','Sit spot provides an opportunity to find a quiet place to observe nature with all of your senses. This opportunity to clear your mind often results in a sense of peace and connection with the natural world.'],['Inside schools building culture','We love being outside and in nature and we also realize that a lot of time is spent inside the four walls of classrooms in schools. We join forces with teachers to bring nature into the classroom, especially when outdoor conditions don’t allow us to be outside.'],['Outside in City parks or on your school grounds','Nature is everywhere, even in the City, and we work with schools to find space to connect with nature. If you are fortunate enough to have access to nature on your schools grounds, we will come to you and help you learn about the local flora and fauna that live outside your door.']];
const overview = [
