---
<BaseLayout title="School Programs" description="Nature connection and social-emotional learning programs for schools."><PageHero eyebrow="Wayfinders for schools" title="School Programs" intro="Wayfinders provides direct service to schools through Professional Development, School-Day Programming (Specials), Extended Day/Enrichment (After School), Field Trips, Clubs, Lunch time Enrichment, Family Circles, and Caregiver & Me." image="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/61532ef9082b334755993cfd/dbc8c4b1-ca3b-4e9f-9b33-459454d7786c/Bard+Faculty+in+Field.jpg?format=1200w" alt="School faculty participating in an outdoor Wayfinders activity"><Button href="mailto:wayfindersonthehudson@gmail.com?subject=School%20Programs">Contact us about school programs</Button></PageHero>
<Section width="wide"><div class="overview">{overview.map(([title, copy]) => <article><h2 class="type-card">{title}</h2><p>{copy}</p></article>)}</div></Section>
<Section width="prose"><p class="lead">Our seasonally based, year-long curriculum ensures that our youth connect with nature and their community around them, and build a bond that encourages them to protect the earth throughout their lives.</p><p>The Wayfinders experience provides rich sensory connections with the natural world that serve as a joyful building block as children grow into their relationship with nature.</p><div class="downloads"><Button href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dXkzFWKMLKDTflatuAs9aJ69WARr7KlO/view?usp=sharing" variant="secondary">K–12 program PDF</Button><Button href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mAGuUsTfBXy0zu5jbDFrRcFXA1RhFE4_/view?usp=drive_link" variant="secondary">Early Childhood PDF</Button></div></Section>
<Section tone="alternate" width="wide"><h2 class="type-section">Ways we work with schools</h2><div class="formats">{formats.map(([title,items])=><article><h3 class="type-card">{title}</h3><ul>{items.map(item=><li>{item}</li>)}</ul></article>)}</div></Section>
<Section width="wide"><h2 class="type-section">Community Building &amp; Faculty Training</h2><div class="approaches">{approaches.map(([title,copy])=><article><h3 class="type-card">{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></article>)}</div></Section>
<Section tone="alternate" width="wide"><div class="gallery">{gallery.map(([image, alt]) => <img src={`https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/61532ef9082b334755993cfd/${image}?format=1200w`} {alt} width="1200" height="800" loading="lazy" />)}</div></Section>
<Section tone="forest" width="prose"><p class="type-label">Wayfinders works with</p><h2 class="type-section">Bard High School Early College (BHSEC)—Bronx</h2><p>Wayfinders partners with Bard High School Early College and their new campus in the Bronx. Through this partnership we provide professional development for the faculty to support teachers who also serve as advisors.</p><p>Wayfinders provides teachers with direct experiences with social emotional learning in preparation and support for the work they are required to do to support students in underserved communities in the Bronx. We also provide direct programming for the school through community days which takes the students out of the building into the local park (Crotona Park) to build nature connection in addition to social emotional learning and community building.</p></Section>
<Section width="prose"><h2 class="type-section">Learn more about our School Programs</h2><p>Wayfinders provides <strong>after-school programs, in-school programs, field trips, and professional development</strong> for schools, including Bard High School Early College - Bronx, Temple Beth Shalom Nursery School and the Shames JCC Early Childhood Center.</p><p>Wayfinders engages children, teachers, and administrators in <strong>nature-based</strong> programming that builds <strong>connection</strong> and <strong>awareness</strong> of our relationship with the natural world while building <strong>community</strong>.</p><p><strong>Social emotional learning</strong> and joyful <strong>adventure</strong> are at the heart of nature connection. Wayfinders integrates fun-filled <strong>team building</strong> adventures into exploration of the natural world so we’re always learning together as a group, and discovering our connections to ourselves and the way we work within our communities as we play.</p><p>Students practice <strong>skill building</strong> which encourages them to get their hands dirty, open their senses, and develop resilience and grit. Along the way, they discover the incredible beauty and peace of the natural world, and find their place in the web of life.</p><Button href="mailto:wayfindersonthehudson@gmail.com?subject=School%20Programs">Contact Us</Button></Section></BaseLayout>
<style>:global(.page-hero .button){margin-top:2rem}.lead{font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.5rem;line-height:1.4}.downloads{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.75rem;margin-top:2rem}.overview,.formats,.approaches,.gallery{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:1rem}.overview article,.formats article,.approaches article{padding:var(--card-padding);border-radius:var(--radius-card);background:var(--color-surface)}.overview article,.approaches article{border:1px solid var(--color-line)}.overview h2,.formats h3,.approaches h3{margin-top:0}.formats li+li{margin-top:.5rem}.gallery img{width:100%;height:22rem;object-fit:cover;border-radius:var(--radius-card)}@media(max-width:47.999rem){.overview,.formats,.approaches,.gallery{grid-template-columns:1fr}.gallery img{height:18rem}.downloads{display:grid}:global(.page-hero .button),.downloads :global(.button){width:100%}}</style>
